INSERT INTO `questions` VALUES (21,'Which biologist has been called `The Darwin of 20th century\'?','Aristotle','Carolus Linnaeus','Ernst Mayr','R.H.Whittaker','C','',4,8,6,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 05:15:51','2025-12-19 05:15:51'),(22,'In plants, growth occurs ______ whereas in animals, it occurs______','only upto a certain age,continuously','continuously,only upto a certain age ','continuously ,continuously','only upto a certain age, only upto a certain age','B','',4,8,6,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 05:25:39','2025-12-19 05:25:39'),(23,'Which two of the below given points are known as the twin characteristics growth ?(i)increase in mass \n(ii) Increase in number of individuals\n(iii) Cellular organisation\n(iv) Cellular differentiation',' (i) and (ii)','(i) and (iii)','(ii) and (iii)',' (iii) and (iv)','A','',4,8,6,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 05:40:27','2025-12-19 05:42:25'),(24,'Two elements P and Q combine to form a compound.\nIf P has 2 and Q has 6 electrons in their outermost shell, what will be formula of the compound formed ?','PQ','P 2 Q ','P2Q3','PQ2','A','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 05:48:51','2025-12-19 05:48:51'),(26,'Which of the following groups consists of organisms which multiply by fragmentation ?','Earthworm, Amoeba, fungi  ','   Earthworm, fungi, bacteria  ',' Fungi, filamentous algae, protonema of mosses','Amoeba, Hydra,bacteria','C','',4,8,6,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 05:51:18','2025-12-19 05:52:47'),(27,'Which of the following groups consists of organisms which multiply by fragmentation ?','Earthworm, Amoeba, fungi  ','   Earthworm, fungi, bacteria  ',' Fungi, filamentous algae, protonema of mosses','Amoeba, Hydra,bacteria','C','',4,8,6,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 05:53:09','2025-12-19 05:53:09'),(28,'How many electrons are involved in the formation of nitrogen molecule?','3','4','8','6','D','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 05:55:20','2025-12-19 05:55:20'),(29,'A pair of electrons present between two identical non-metals','is shifted to one of the atoms ','is shared equally between them','undergoes addition reactions','have same spin','B','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 05:59:04','2025-12-19 05:59:04'),(30,'Which of the following organisms do not reproduce?','Mules ','Mules  B Sterile worker bees  C Infertile human couples  D All of these',' Infertile human females  ','All of these','D','',4,8,6,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 06:03:56','2025-12-19 06:03:56'),(31,'In which of the following molecules octet rule is not followed?',' NH3','CH4',' CO2',' NO','D','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 06:04:08','2025-12-19 06:04:08'),(32,'In a covalent bond formation',' transfer of electrons','EQUAL SHARING OF ELECTRONS BETWEEN TWO ATOMS TAKES PLAE','electrons are shared by one atom only','electrons are donated by one atom and shared both atoms','B','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 06:10:51','2025-12-19 06:10:51'),(33,'During a coordinate bond formation:','During a co One electron from an atom is transferred to other ',' One electron is lost from both the atoms',' A pair of electrons are contributed by one atom and shared by both the atoms','A pair of electrons are transferred to the other atom','C','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 06:15:26','2025-12-19 06:15:26'),(34,'Growth cannot be taken as a defining property of living organisms because','all living organisms do not show growth','non-living things also grow from inside',' non-living things also grow by increasing in mass','some living organisms do not show process of reproduction','D','',4,8,6,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 06:17:42','2025-12-19 06:17:42'),(35,'Which of the following molecules contains covalent and coordinate bonds?','CCl4',' H2SO4','NaCl','Mg(OH)2','B','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 06:20:11','2025-12-19 06:20:11'),(36,'Which of the following statements regarding the response of living organisms to external stimuli is correct?','The external environmental stimuli can be physical, chemical or biological.','All organisms from the prokaryotes to the most complex eukaryotes can sense and respond to environmental stimuli.','Consciousness and response to external stimuli is the defining property of living organisms.','All of these.','D','',4,8,6,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 06:22:44','2025-12-19 06:22:44'),(37,'Among the following the exceptions of the octet rule is','the incomplete octet of central atom','an odd number of electrons on central atom','expanded octet of the central atom ','all of these','D','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 07:39:30','2025-12-19 07:39:30'),(38,'Two elements X and Y combine to form a compound XY. Under what conditions the bond formed between them will be ionic?','If the difference in electronegativities of X and Y is 1.9','If the difference in electronegativities of X and Y is more than 1.9','If the difference in electronegativities of X and Y is less than 1.79','If both X and Y are highly electronegative','B','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 07:43:02','2025-12-19 07:43:59'),(39,'In which of the following species the bond is non- directional?','NCl3','RbCl ','BeCl2','BeCl3','B','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 07:47:00','2025-12-19 07:47:00'),(40,'Which of the following elements forms predominantly covalent compounds as compared to other elements which form ionic compounds?','Be','Mg','Ca','Sr','A','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 08:15:14','2025-12-19 08:15:14'),(41,'Which of the following molecules does not show any reasoning structures?','NH3','CO3 2-','O3','SO3','A','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 08:26:22','2025-12-19 08:26:22'),(42,'The canonical or resonating structures of a molecule required to describe the structure of a molecule follow which of the following rules?','The relative position of all atoms can differ 22%','The same number of unpaired and paired electrons in all structures','The energy of each structure is different','Like charges are present on adjacent atoms','B','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 08:29:42','2025-12-19 08:29:42'),(43,'Which of the following statements is not true regarding molecular orbital theory?','The atomic orbitals of comparable energies combine to form molecular orbitals','An atomic orbital is monocentric while a molecular orbital is polycentric',' Bonding molecular orbital has higher energy than antibonding molecular orbital.','Molecular orbitals like atomic orbitals obey Aufbau principle for filling of electrons.','C','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 08:36:57','2025-12-19 08:36:57'),(44,'The conditions for the combination of atomic orbitals to form molecular orbitals are stated below. Mark the incorrect condition mentioned here.','The combining atomic orbitals must have nearly same energy','The combining atomic orbitals must overlap to the maximum extent ','The combining atomic orbitals must have same symmetry about the molecular axis','Pi molecular orbitals are symmetrical around the bond axis','B','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 08:46:50','2025-12-19 08:46:50'),(45,'Which of the following bond orders is indication of existence of a molecule?','Zero bond order','Negative bond order','Positive bond order ','All of these','C','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 08:49:20','2025-12-19 08:49:20'),(46,'Which of the following facts regarding bond order is not valid?','Bond order is given by the number of bonds between the two atoms in a molecule ','With increase in bond order, bond enthalpy of the molecule decreases','Isoelectronic molecules and ions have identical bond orders','With increase in bond order, bond length decreases','B','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 08:52:29','2025-12-19 08:52:29'),(47,'Paramagnetism is shown by the molecules which have','paired electrons','unpaired electrons','lone pair of electrons','bond order more than one','B','',4,21,NULL,'NEET',NULL,1,NULL,'2025-12-19 08: